{
  "title": "Blend: fold, hoist, check bounds",
  "about": [
    "The running example of the spec: a constant to fold, an",
    "expression to hoist out of the loop, and a bounds check on every",
    "charCodeAt."
  ],
  "group": "Start here",
  "pipeline": "O2",
  "inputs": {
    "blend": {
      "work": { "buffer": [40, 40], "cell": [0, 255] },
      "n": [0, 40],
      "a": [-100, 100],
      "b": [-100, 100]
    }
  },
  "chapter": "welcome",
  "focus": 5,
  "try": [
    [
      "Why does the bounds check on work.charCodeAt(i) survive O2",
      "here?"
    ],
    [
      "Change the loop bound to work.length in a new project and show",
      "me what bce does."
    ]
  ]
}
function blend(work: buffer, n: i32, a: i32, b: i32): i32 {
    const scale = 4 * 16;
    let s = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i = i + 1) {
        s = s + work.charCodeAt(i) * (a * b + scale);
    }
    return s / 8;
}
After O2, select the hoisted statement in the IR view: its why() names
the loop fact that made the move valid. The bounds check stays, because
the loop runs to n, not to work.length.
